---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';

// DRAFT for the organiser to review. Items in [square brackets] need filling in
// (also listed in PLACEHOLDERS.md). This is not legal advice.
const updated = '11 November 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How Derby Gala Dinner collects and uses your personal information.">
  <PageHeader title="Privacy policy" />

  <section class="policy bg-bars">
    <div class="policy__inner container">
      <p class="policy__updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p class="policy__lede">
        This policy explains how VOLT7 ("we", "us") collects and uses personal information through the Derby Gala
        Dinner website, derbygaladinner.co.uk.
      </p>

      <h2 class="label gold">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Derby Gala Dinner is organised by VOLT7, 8 Mallard Way, Pride Park, Derby DE24 8GX, to raise funds for Bridge The Gap. We are
        responsible for the personal information you give us through this website. If you have any questions about this policy
        or your information, email us at <a href="mailto:hello@volt7.agency">hello@volt7.agency</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="label gold">What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you send us an enquiry or a message through the website, we collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name (and your title, if you give it)</li>
        <li>your email address, and your phone number if you give it</li>
        <li>your company name and company address, if you give them</li>
        <li>what you are enquiring about (the table type, or the types of sponsorship you are interested in)</li>
        <li>anything you write in the message box on the general enquiry form</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not take payments or collect card details on this website.</p>

      <h2 class="label gold">How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>to reply to your enquiry</li>
        <li>to arrange table bookings and sponsorship, including sending invoices</li>
        <li>if you book, to contact you about the event, such as menu choices and dietary requirements</li>
        <li>to tell you about future Derby Gala Dinner events and promotions</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We never sell your details. If you would rather not hear from us about future events and promotions, email
        <a href="mailto:hello@volt7.agency">hello@volt7.agency</a> and we will stop.
      </p>

      <h2 class="label gold">Our legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK data protection law (UK GDPR), we use your information because you have asked us to take steps before
        entering into an agreement with you (a booking or sponsorship), and because we have a legitimate interest in
        responding to enquiries about the event and in telling people who have enquired about future events.
      </p>

      <h2 class="label gold">Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We use a small number of service providers to run the website:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Resend</strong> delivers form submissions to our email inbox. The Resend account is managed by Zap Digital,
          who built and maintain this website for us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc.) checks that form submissions come from a person and not a
          spam bot. It processes information such as your IP address and browser details to do this.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Adobe Fonts</strong> provides the fonts used on the website.</li>
        <li><strong>IONOS</strong> hosts the website.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some of these providers are based outside the UK. Where your information is transferred outside the UK, it is protected
        by the safeguards that UK data protection law requires.
      </p>

      <h2 class="label gold">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiries that do not lead to a booking for up to [12 months]. If you book a table or sponsor the event, we keep
        your details for as long as we need them to run the event and to meet our legal and accounting obligations (usually
        [6 years] for invoices).
      </p>

      <h2 class="label gold">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to ask for a copy of the information we hold about you, and to ask us to correct it, delete it,
        restrict how we use it, or stop using it. To do any of these, email <a href="mailto:hello@volt7.agency">hello@volt7.agency</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office
        (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a> or on 0303 123
        1113.
      </p>

      <h2 class="label gold" id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not set any cookies of its own, and we do not use analytics or advertising cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you open an enquiry form, <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> loads to protect the form from spam. It may store
        information in your browser that is needed for this security check.
      </p>
      <p>
        To stop the forms being misused, the website also keeps a scrambled record of how many enquiries have come from each
        visitor. It cannot be read back as an IP address and is cleared within a day.
      </p>
      <p>
        The "View on maps" link on the event details page opens Google Maps in a new tab. Google's own
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a> applies there.
      </p>

      <h2 class="label gold">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy, we will update it on this page and change the date at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy {
    padding: calc(100 * var(--u)) 0 calc(160 * var(--u));
  }

  .policy__inner {
    max-width: calc(985 * var(--u) + 2 * var(--gutter));
  }

  .policy__inner > * + * {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .policy__inner > h2 {
    margin-top: 48px;
  }

  .policy__updated {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
  }

  .policy__lede {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: calc(max(22px, calc(36 * var(--u))) * var(--type-scale));
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .policy ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .policy a {
    color: var(--gold);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .policy {
      padding: 48px 0 80px;
    }

    .policy__inner {
      max-width: none;
    }
  }
</style>
